Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:56:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] Helpers behind a wrapper that only widens its arguments

A support function can be a wrapper that widens its 32-bit arguments and jumps
to the function doing the work: SZArrayNew(klass, uint32 length) is
"mov edx, edx; jmp Array::NewSpecific". A library recognizes the wrapper, but
whole-program optimized code mostly calls the function behind it directly, and
that call stayed an unidentified native call with the class used as data. The
function jumped to is now the same helper (HelperShapes; off with
REWIND_NO_WIDENED_HELPERS). It does what the wrapper does for every argument the
wrapper passes on; nothing is taken over where something is already known, nor
for compiled methods or wrappers that do more than widen a register into itself.

rewind-lab's helpers (hir, norm, ir, ...) now also go through the same
completion as the decompiler (code shapes, then roles).

Unity 6000.0.60f1 Master game read with the 6000.0.85f2 library: whole game
12,759 of 19,693 complete (was 12,403); its own assembly 2,169 of 2,968 (was 2,114).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
